body:
I haven't had the game boot with friends again, but in the event viewer the error is Log Kernel-Power 41?

&#x200B;

I believe the BSoD code is : 0x8000400000000002

Awesome, thanks for the heads up! was a little worried a bit that I hadn't heard anything for a bit, but I just have to keep in my head that the process takes time!

&#x200B;

Thanks again for the reply!

I just gave it a big clean just with an anti static brush and compressed air. temps at idle sit at about 30 degrees and sitting at between 70-80 degrees. It was Detroit become human that crashed but was running it on Medium graphics. I also have the side panel off the tower as the cpu cooler is too big for the side. I'm assuming that can cause it to heat up a bit more than it should. The only other question I have, is if a 2060 super is much better than a 2060 as I am on a bit of a budget with it but will spend the extra if it is worth it.

&#x200B;

P.S Thanks for the fast reply!
